        <p>-AjOTICE IS HEREBY GIVEN, that the next GEN- II ERAL QUARTER SESSIONS of the Peace for the COUNTY OF CHESTER will ne holden at the COURT HOUSE, NETHER KNUTSFORD, in and for the said County, on MONIIAY. the 16,11 day of October next, at Half-past Eleven in the Forenoon, when the Grand Jury will be empannelled. The hearing of all appeals arising within the Hun- dreds of Bucklow, Macclesfield, and Northwich, form- ing the Knutsford District, and the trials of all prisoners committed from such Hundreds, will take place at such Sessions. The Grand and Petty Jury tor the Knutsford District must be in attendance at the Court House, Knutsford, at the opening of the Court on MONDAY, the 16th day of October, at Half-past Eleven o'clock in the Forenoon. THE Court will be adjourned to the Castle of Chester, on THURSDAY, the 19th day of October next, at Eleven o'clock in the Forenoon, when another Grand Jury will be ernpannelled. The hearing of all Appeals arising within the Hundreds of Broxton, Eddisbury, Nantwic/C. and Wirral, forming the Chester District, and the trials of all prisoners committed from the last-mentioned Hundreds will take place at such Adjourned Sessir;ms. The Grand and Petty Jury for the Chester District must be in attendance at the Castle of Chi. tar, at the opening of the Court on THURSDAY, the 19th day of October next, at Eleven o'clock in the Forenoon, REGINALD POTTS, Clerk of the Peace for the County of Chester Chester, 25th September, 1893.</p>
